url: "https://sstoeckl.github.io/populism-llm/"
abstract: >
  Replication code for "The Milei question, or: How liberal are right-wing
  populist parties? A measurement approach using large language models." The
  pipeline scores European party manifestos on populism and liberalism
  dimensions using three independent LLM families (Claude Sonnet 4.6,
  GPT-4.1-mini, Gemini 3.5 Flash) and computes a specification-curve robustness
  analysis across the full grid of defensible analytic choices.
keywords:
  - populism
  - liberalism
  - large language models
  - party manifestos
  - specification curve
  - non-standard errors
  - cross-validation
